_model: other_work
---
title: Constructions
---
order: 4
---
body:

Every construction the library implements, each with a figure you can drag.
The signature and description of each are taken from the library's own
reference table, so this page and the source cannot drift apart silently.

An element is declared as a single string:

```
name;type;construction;arguments;nameColor;vertexColor;edgeColor;faceColor
```

The four colour fields are optional, and `0` means transparent. `{A}` in the
prose lights the matching element in the figure beside it — see
[Using geomlib diagrams](/geomlib/using/).

> **A note on the signatures.** When a line's name appears in an argument list
> it expands to its two endpoints, so `params: ["AB"]` arrives as two points,
> not one. The signatures below are written post-expansion, which is why some
> read as more points than you would write.

## Point constructions

### `point;free`
**Signature** — ``int x, int y``  
Freely draggable point.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_free" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_free",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,60",
            "B;point;free;180,110"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Draggable anywhere. Red by default.

```
B;point;free;180,110
```

### `point;fixed`
**Signature** — ``int x, int y [, int z]``  
Non-draggable fixed point (2D and 3D variants).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_fixed" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_fixed",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;fixed;120,80",
            "A;point;free;60,130"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Not draggable; the anchor other things hang off.

```
O;point;fixed;120,80
```

### `point;first`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B``  
Returns point A (first endpoint of a line).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_first" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_first",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,120",
            "B;point;free;190,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "F;point;first;AB"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The first endpoint of a line, as a point in its own right.

```
F;point;first;AB
```

### `point;last`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B``  
Returns point B (last endpoint of a line).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_last" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_last",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,120",
            "B;point;free;190,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "L;point;last;AB"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The other endpoint.

```
L;point;last;AB
```

### `point;midpoint`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B``  
Midpoint of segment AB.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_midpoint" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_midpoint",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,120",
            "B;point;free;190,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "M;point;midpoint;A,B"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Bisects the segment — drag either end.

```
M;point;midpoint;A,B
```

### `point;intersection`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C, D [, Plane]``  
Intersection of lines AB and CD.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_intersection" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_intersection",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;40,40",
            "B;point;free;200,130",
            "C;point;free;40,130",
            "D;point;free;200,40",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "X;point;intersection;A,B,C,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Where two lines cross.

```
X;point;intersection;A,B,C,D
```

### `point;foot`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B, Point C``  
Foot of perpendicular from A to line BC.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_foot" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_foot",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "B;point;free;40,140",
            "C;point;free;210,140",
            "A;point;free;110,40",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "M;point;foot;A,B,C",
            "AM;line;connect;A,M;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Foot of the perpendicular from a point to a line.

```
M;point;foot;A,B,C
```

### `point;extend`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C, D``  
Point E on line AB so BE = CD.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_extend" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_extend",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,110",
            "B;point;free;130,110",
            "C;point;free;50,160",
            "D;point;free;110,160",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "E;point;extend;A,B,C,D",
            "BE;line;connect;B,E;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Lays off |CD| beyond B — Euclid I.3.

```
E;point;extend;A,B,C,D
```

### `point;cutoff`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C, D``  
Point E on line AB so AE = CD.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_cutoff" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_cutoff",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,110",
            "B;point;free;200,110",
            "C;point;free;50,160",
            "D;point;free;110,160",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "E;point;cutoff;A,B,C,D",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Cuts |CD| off from A along AB.

```
E;point;cutoff;A,B,C,D
```

### `point;center`
**Signature** — ``Circle A``  
Center of circle A.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_center" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_center",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,90",
            "P;point;free;190,90",
            "circ;circle;radius;O,P",
            "Z;point;center;circ"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Recovers a circle's centre as a point.

```
Z;point;center;circ
```

### `point;circumcenter`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C [, Plane]``  
Circumcenter of triangle ABC (2D and 3D variants).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_circumcenter" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_circumcenter",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;70,40",
            "B;point;free;40,140",
            "C;point;free;200,120",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "O;point;circumcenter;A,B,C"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Equidistant from all three vertices.

```
O;point;circumcenter;A,B,C
```

### `point;lineSlider`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, int x, int y [, int z]``  
Point draggable along line AB (2D, 3D, segment variants).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_lineSlider" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_lineSlider",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;40,130",
            "B;point;free;210,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "P;point;lineSlider;A,B,120,95"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Draggable, but only along the line. Orange.

```
P;point;lineSlider;A,B,120,95
```

### `point;circleSlider`
**Signature** — ``Circle A, int x, int y [, int z]``  
Point draggable along circle A.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_circleSlider" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_circleSlider",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,95",
            "R;point;free;190,95",
            "circ;circle;radius;O,R",
            "P;point;circleSlider;circ,60,60"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Draggable around the circle.

```
P;point;circleSlider;circ,60,60
```

### `point;perpendicular`
**Signature** — `Various (5 signature variants)`  
Point D s.t. AD ⊥ AB and \.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_perpendicular" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_perpendicular",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,140",
            "B;point;free;200,140",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "D;point;perpendicular;A,B",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

A point square to AB at A.

```
D;point;perpendicular;A,B
```

### `point;parallelogram`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B, Point C``  
4th vertex D of parallelogram ABCD (D = A+C−B).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_parallelogram" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_parallelogram",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,50",
            "B;point;free;40,140",
            "C;point;free;180,150",
            "D;point;parallelogram;A,B,C",
            "ABCD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;0;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The fourth vertex: D = A + C − B.

```
D;point;parallelogram;A,B,C
```

### `point;vertex`
**Signature** — ``Polygon P, int i``  
i-th vertex of polygon P.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_point_vertex" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_point_vertex",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,60",
            "B;point;free;170,120",
            "sq;polygon;square;A,B;0;0;black;cyan",
            "V;point;vertex;sq,3"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Pulls the i-th vertex out of a polygon.

```
V;point;vertex;sq,3
```

## Line constructions

### `line;connect`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B``  
Line through A and B.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_connect" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_connect",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,120",
            "B;point;free;190,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The straightedge between two points.

```
AB;line;connect;A,B
```

### `line;extend`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C, D``  
Line extending AB by length CD.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_extend" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_extend",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,120",
            "B;point;free;140,90",
            "C;point;free;60,160",
            "D;point;free;120,160",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "AE;line;extend;A,B,C,D;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

AB produced by a further |CD|.

```
AE;line;extend;A,B,C,D;0;0;red
```

### `line;parallel`
**Signature** — ``Point A, Point B, Point C``  
Line through A parallel and equal to line BC.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_parallel" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_parallel",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,140",
            "B;point;free;200,140",
            "P;point;free;110,60",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "par;line;parallel;P,A,B;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Through P, parallel to AB.

```
par;line;parallel;P,A,B;0;0;red
```

### `line;perpendicular`
**Signature** — `Various (5 signature variants)`  
Line perpendicular to another.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_perpendicular" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_perpendicular",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,130",
            "B;point;free;200,130",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "perp;line;perpendicular;A,B;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Square to AB at A.

```
perp;line;perpendicular;A,B;0;0;red
```

### `line;bichord`
**Signature** — ``Circle A, Circle B``  
Line connecting two circle intersections.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_bichord" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_bichord",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O1;point;free;90,95",
            "R1;point;free;150,95",
            "O2;point;free;160,95",
            "R2;point;free;225,95",
            "c1;circle;radius;O1,R1;0;0;0;0",
            "c2;circle;radius;O2,R2;0;0;0;0",
            "ch;line;bichord;c1,c2;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The common chord of two circles.

```
ch;line;bichord;c1,c2;0;0;red
```

### `line;chord`
**Signature** — ``Point B, Point C, Circle A``  
Chord of circle A cut by line BC.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_line_chord" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_line_chord",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,95",
            "R;point;free;195,95",
            "circ;circle;radius;O,R",
            "A;point;free;70,60",
            "B;point;free;170,150",
            "ch;line;chord;A,B,circ;0;0;red"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The chord line AB cuts from a circle.

```
ch;line;chord;A,B,circ;0;0;red
```

## Circle constructions

### `circle;radius`
**Signature** — ``Point center, Point edge [, Point C]``  
Circle with center and radius; 2-point (radius=\.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_circle_radius" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_circle_radius",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,95",
            "P;point;free;195,95",
            "circ;circle;radius;O,P"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Centre and a point on it — Euclid's compass.

```
circ;circle;radius;O,P
```

### `circle;circumcircle`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C [, Plane]``  
Circle through three points (2D and 3D).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_circle_circumcircle" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_circle_circumcircle",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;70,40",
            "B;point;free;40,140",
            "C;point;free;200,130",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "circ;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;red;0"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Through all three vertices.

```
circ;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;red;0
```

## Polygon constructions

### `polygon;triangle`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C``  
Triangle with vertices A, B, C.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_triangle" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_triangle",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;110,40",
            "B;point;free;40,150",
            "C;point;free;190,150",
            "t;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Three vertices.

```
t;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;cyan
```

### `polygon;quadrilateral`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C, D``  
Quadrilateral ABCD.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_quadrilateral" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_quadrilateral",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,40",
            "B;point;free;40,150",
            "C;point;free;190,150",
            "D;point;free;200,50",
            "q;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Four, in order.

```
q;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;cyan
```

### `polygon;parallelogram`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C``  
Parallelogram ABCD where D = A+(C−B).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_parallelogram" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_parallelogram",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;60,50",
            "B;point;free;40,150",
            "C;point;free;180,150",
            "p;polygon;parallelogram;A,B,C;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Three vertices; the fourth follows.

```
p;polygon;parallelogram;A,B,C;0;0;black;cyan
```

### `polygon;square`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B``  
Square on side AB.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_square" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_square",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;70,60",
            "B;point;free;170,90",
            "s;polygon;square;A,B;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Built on one side — Euclid I.46.

```
s;polygon;square;A,B;0;0;black;cyan
```

### `polygon;equilateralTriangle`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B [, Plane]``  
Equilateral triangle on side AB (2D + 3D).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_equilateralTriangle" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_equilateralTriangle",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;70,140",
            "B;point;free;180,140",
            "t;polygon;equilateralTriangle;A,B;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Euclid I.1. Vertex order picks the apex side.

```
t;polygon;equilateralTriangle;A,B;0;0;black;cyan
```

### `polygon;regularPolygon`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B [, Plane], int n``  
Regular n-gon on edge AB (2D + 3D).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_polygon_regularPolygon" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_polygon_regularPolygon",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,95",
            "A;point;free;190,95",
            "p;polygon;regularPolygon;O,A,7;0;0;black;cyan"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

N-gon about a centre — here seven sides.

```
p;polygon;regularPolygon;O,A,7;0;0;black;cyan
```

## Sector constructions

### `sector;sector`
**Signature** — ``Point A, B, C [, Plane]``  
Circular sector from center through A and B (2 variants).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_sector_sector" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_sector_sector",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "V;point;free;60,150",
            "A;point;free;200,150",
            "B;point;free;150,50",
            "VA;line;connect;V,A",
            "VB;line;connect;V,B",
            "s;sector;sector;V,A,B;0;0;magenta;magenta"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

A wedge between two arms.

```
s;sector;sector;V,A,B;0;0;magenta;magenta
```

### `sector;angleMarker`
**Signature** — ``Point V, P1, P2 [, int radiusPx]``  
Interior angle marker at V — element-chosen radius (default 22px, clamped to 0.45× shorter arm), auto-interior, translucent palette fill.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_sector_angleMarker" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_sector_angleMarker",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "V;point;free;60,150",
            "A;point;free;200,150",
            "B;point;free;150,50",
            "VA;line;connect;V,A",
            "VB;line;connect;V,B",
            "m;sector;angleMarker;V,A,B;0;0;magenta;magenta"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

The small arc marking an angle. Auto-orients to the interior.

```
m;sector;angleMarker;V,A,B;0;0;magenta;magenta
```

### `sector;arc`
**Signature** — ``Point A, M, B [, Plane]``  
Arc of circle passing through A, M, B (M is on the arc, 2D + 3D).

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="c_sector_arc" width="260" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "c_sector_arc",
        background: "0,0,100",
        elements: [
            "O;point;free;120,120",
            "A;point;free;200,120",
            "B;point;free;120,45",
            "a;sector;arc;O,A,B;0;0;red;0"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Arc of a circle between two points.

```
a;sector;arc;O,A,B;0;0;red;0
```
